Licensing of the reproducibility package
========================================

Package of the paper "SPECTRA: An Ontology and Benchmark for 3GPP Traceability
[Experiment, Analysis & Benchmark]".
Repository: https://github.com/spectra-ontology/spec-trace

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Material written by the project: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International (CC BY 4.0, SPDX: CC-BY-4.0)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Scope: every file of this package.

  - code/ and restore/: the build, benchmark, gate, scoring, analysis and
    restore scripts;
  - ontology/: the OWL ontology and its SHACL shapes;
  - records/ and sqlite/: the identifier, code, date, link, hash and locator
    fields of the records, in JSON-LD and SQLite;
  - receipts/: the identity-review receipts;
  - benchmark/ and abstention/: the questions, requested fields, gold rows,
    evidence lists, anchor lists and gate reports;
  - responses/ and diagnosis/: the stored responses, queries, scores, run
    records and per-item miss classifications;
  - docs/: release 1.2.0 of the ontology and its documentation pages;
  - sources/manifest.jsonl, the root-level redaction lists, the datasheet,
    the README and CITATION.cff.

These components are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0).

You are free to:
  - Share: copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format.
  - Adapt: remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose,
           even commercially.

Under the following terms:
  - Attribution: You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the
                 license, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so
                 in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that suggests
                 the licensor endorses you or your use.

Appropriate credit: cite the paper named above and the authors listed in
CITATION.cff of the repository.

Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. 3GPP documents: restored by the user, under their own terms
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The package holds no text of 3GPP documents. It refers to TDocs, change
requests, meeting reports and Technical Specifications by identifier and
archive path, and it cites meeting reports by archive path, SHA-256 and
locator. Archive file names stay as the 3GPP archive publishes them.

restore/restore_sources.py fetches the meeting reports listed in
sources/manifest.jsonl from the public 3GPP archive (https://www.3gpp.org/ftp/)
onto the user's machine and checks them against the recorded hashes. The
restored files, and any text taken from them, are 3GPP material. They stay
under the terms of 3GPP and its Organizational Partners and are outside the
licence of section 1:

  - https://www.3gpp.org/about-us/legal-matters
  - https://www.3gpp.org/about-us/3gpp-faqs
  - https://www.3gpp.org/terms-of-use

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Contact and corrections
----------------------------------------------------------------------

For licensing questions, attribution corrections, or rights clarifications,
file an issue at https://github.com/spectra-ontology/spec-trace/issues.
